{
  "name": "cast_prompts_v2",
  "description": "Frozen v2 prompt set, two axes, 16 categories x 8 prompts = 128. Form axis: 4 clear categories (SG, MU, AT, TM) + 4 ambiguous categories (AB, IM, UN, LX). Domain axis: 8 sound domains (VO, EN, MS, NA, MC, HL, CU, FX), each built from 4 clear<->ambiguous pairs (pair_of) describing the same target sound; EN also has space contrasts (contrast_of). core=true marks 4 prompts per category (64 total). Frozen before generation; never edited after results are seen.",
  "hypothesis": "Pre-declared before generation: the PLADIS gain over dense attention (CLAP, AQAScore, event-level AQAScore) is larger for ambiguous prompts than for clear prompts, tested (1) across form-axis categories (AB, IM, UN, LX vs SG, MU, AT, TM) and (2) within domain-axis clear<->ambiguous pairs.",
